### Security requirements
- Hash passwords with bcryptjs.
- Use JWT expiration.
- Validate all inputs on the server.
- Enforce permissions in backend middleware, not only in the UI.
- Prevent institutions from accessing other institutions' records.
- Do not store plaintext passwords.
- Do not hardcode secrets.
- Do not provide public self-registration with privileged roles.
- If public institution registration is supported, assign only the INSTITUTION role and require verification.
- Use secure session handling and avoid storing sensitive tokens in localStorage where possible.
- Never ship development demo credentials into a production deployment.

Provide a development-only seed script for sample users. Require explicit opt-in for seeding and disable demo seeding by default in production.

